  "query_preview": "(Sunday through Wednesday)...\nThe warming will continue for inland areas on Sunday with high\ntemperatures on Sunday 5 to 10 degrees above average for most\nareas. Sunday high temperatures will range from the lower 70s \nnear the coast to the lower to mid 80s for the Inland Empire with \nthe lower to mid 90s for the lower deserts.\n\nFor Monday through Wednesday, a low pressure system will move\ntoward the California coast and inland into California with\ncontinued model differences with the timing as well as with the\nweakening that may occur as it moves inland. For southwestern\nCalifornia, it will be cooler and breezier. NBM chances for \nmeasurable precipitation remain less than 20 percent and are \ngreatest for late Monday night into Tuesday morning.",
